    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d467-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d467-f1-content"> Authorship not
                indicated. A copy of this document in the Hiss Collection, which embodies the
                alterations written on the copy reproduced above, bears the following handwritten
                notations: <p>“Mr. Early took original 2/11 10.30 a. m. &amp; said he would send
                    it.”</p>
                <p>“Map room informed us about 1.30 p. m. that it had been sent.”</p>
                <p>A copy of the same telegram obtained from the Roosevelt Papers indicates that the
                    time of release was to be twenty-four, rather than forty-eight, hours after
                    publication of the communiqué.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
